# Household fail-closed RAG patch.
# Open WebUI commit: 8bd8b4fac5e059578ac0c74b3c18d11139f88b7d
# Open WebUI 0.11.4 sdist SHA-256: 1f1a31668a0dee733953c29d6183d78dd78984e696aa8eb0f2083f5796497be0
# The package installs open-webui-rag-gate.py as open_webui/retrieval/rag_gate.py before build.
# App startup remains available for ordinary chat when qualification fails; authenticated /api/v1/retrieval/health stays 503.
# Gate scope: knowledge-base content and anything attached to a model or folder as knowledge. Unattached notes, chats, and memories are personal data outside it.
# Gate closed: a chat with any attachment returns the 503 detail. The builtin query_*_files, grep_*_files, view_file, and view_knowledge_file tools, and view_note for a knowledge-attached note, return it as a tool error; search_notes omits knowledge-attached notes.
# Gate qualified: explicitly requested content is allowed whole, including full-context items and text, note, chat, and url attachments; search results are reranked. The global full-context and bypass modes stay refused.
# Hybrid-search errors: when hybrid search raises anything but RAGUnavailableError, the request fails with the gate's 503 instead of upstream's unreranked vector-search fallback, and the gate stays qualified.
# Empty candidates: RerankCompressor keeps 0.11.4's early return of [] without calling the reranker. Nothing unreranked reaches chat, and closing the gate on an empty knowledge base would only cause an outage.
# tests/test_open_webui_household_rag_gate.py pins each of these.
